@startuml

note across

Scenario 3 – Contextual Route Description

"This sequence diagram illustrates the generation of a contextual
description for previously generated route candidates.

The API Layer requests the Geospatial Engine to derive the relevant
context. The Geospatial Engine determines a shared contextual area
covering the route candidates, obtains the required contextual data
through Data Management, and correlates that data with each route."

end note


participant "API Layer" as API
participant "Geospatial Engine" as GE
participant "Data Management" as DM
participant "Meteo Data Source" as Meteo
participant "Open Data Source" as OpenData


API -> GE : I_GeospatialService:\ngetRoutesContext(routes : RouteCandidates)

GE -> GE : Analyze route candidate geometries
GE -> GE : Build shared context area

GE -> GE : Derive WeatherDataRequest\nfrom shared context area
GE -> DM : I_ContextDataAccess:\ngetWeatherData(weatherRequest)

DM -> Meteo : I_MeteoDataAccess:\nfetchWeatherData(area, time)
Meteo --> DM : WeatherData
DM --> GE : WeatherData

GE -> GE : Derive UrbanDataRequest\nfrom shared context area
GE -> DM : I_ContextDataAccess:\ngetUrbanData(urbanDataRequest)

DM -> OpenData : I_OpenDataAccess:\nfetchUrbanData(area, dataType)
OpenData --> DM : UrbanData
DM --> GE : UrbanData

GE -> GE : Correlate contextual data\nwith each route candidate
GE -> GE : Build RouteContext\nfor each route
GE -> GE : Build ContextDescription

GE --> API : I_GeospatialService:\nContextDescription

@enduml